{
  "paragraphs": [
    "alarms: 118 of 118 rows have known values (100.0% coverage).",
    "At k = 20, mean shared-label agreement is 93.8% when weighting positive anchor\u2013label pairs, and 93.7% when weighting labels equally. Mean individual label lift is 2.304 and equal-label lift is 2.603. Mean lift is not aggregate purity divided by aggregate chance.",
    "pressure: 74 known positives; 74 evaluable positive anchors have 94.1% mean agreement, versus 62.7% reference prevalence (lift 1.5). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "hot: 35 known positives; 35 evaluable positive anchors have 93.6% mean agreement, versus 29.7% reference prevalence (lift 3.155). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "vibration: 35 known positives; 35 evaluable positive anchors have 93.6% mean agreement, versus 29.7% reference prevalence (lift 3.155). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "Known-neighbor coverage at this k is 100.0%. Unknown neighbors are excluded from agreement denominators; missing annotations can bias the result.",
    "The saved null comparison gives an empirical one-sided p-value of 0.25 for macro_lift. This tests the specified shuffle, not semantic understanding; use the combined multiple-testing table and practical effect sizes when judging the finding.",
    "The probe panel measures recoverability on a held-out split. Compare each model with its baseline; recoverability and nearest-neighbor usefulness answer different questions.",
    "baseline: balanced_accuracy 0.5, macro_f1 0.4038; 30 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "linear: balanced_accuracy 0.969, macro_f1 0.9621; 30 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "For paired_micro_purity at k = 20, A is 0.9382 and B is 0.9278, with B\u2212A -0.01042 across 109 paired anchors. Conditional 95% interval: -0.01639 to -0.004875; higher is better for this measure. This does not rank overall embedding quality.",
    "Embedding A normalization comparison on identical held-out rows: raw_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.969, unit: balanced_accuracy 0.969, unit_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.969, norm_only: balanced_accuracy 0.5159. Direction-only and magnitude-only scores describe accessible information for these pipelines; fit telemetry does not establish encoder-training stability.",
    "Embedding B normalization comparison on identical held-out rows: raw_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.9602, unit: balanced_accuracy 0.969, unit_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.9602, norm_only: balanced_accuracy 0.5159. Direction-only and magnitude-only scores describe accessible information for these pipelines; fit telemetry does not establish encoder-training stability.",
    "In the raw_euclidean filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the raw_euclidean filtration for embedding B, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the unit_chordal filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 3 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the unit_chordal filtration for embedding B, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "Next: compare feature measurements across scales, check probe gains against baselines, or summarize a selected region. Shared labels and correlated features can suggest patterns, but do not establish why the model retrieved an item."
